368
00:23:55,961 --> 00:24:00,440
Our pick at number five is a weird weapon designed to literally knock the bad guys off

369
00:24:00,441 --> 00:24:06,400
their feet, the mobility denial system.

370
00:24:06,401 --> 00:24:09,004
This strange weapon has been developed for the U.S.

371
00:24:09,005 --> 00:24:10,740
military by the Southwest Research

372
00:24:10,741 --> 00:24:15,280
Institute in San Antonio, Texas.

373
00:24:15,281 --> 00:24:19,360
an anti-traction material that can turn just about any surface

374
00:24:19,361 --> 00:24:21,740
into a slip and slide.

375
00:24:21,741 --> 00:24:24,180
The idea is to trip up aggressors trying

376
00:24:24,181 --> 00:24:29,760
to enter restricted areas, like embassies and military bases.

377
00:24:29,761 --> 00:24:32,380
The anti-traction material provides the military

378
00:24:32,381 --> 00:24:36,040
with the way of providing a standoff distance between them

379
00:24:36,041 --> 00:24:37,220
and a riotous crowd.

380
00:24:40,320 --> 00:24:43,000
This is the anti-traction material powder in a dry form.

381
00:24:43,001 --> 00:24:45,000
It's an acrylamide polymer.

382
00:24:45,001 --> 00:24:50,400
Similar to in consistency to salt, it's very fine.

383
00:24:50,401 --> 00:24:55,380
We'll mix a little bit up here, pour a little water in.

384
00:24:55,381 --> 00:24:59,520
You can see it immediately starts to absorb the water.

385
00:24:59,521 --> 00:25:04,420
It becomes this gelatinous mass that is very, very slimy

386
00:25:04,421 --> 00:25:06,280
and slippery.

387
00:25:06,281 --> 00:25:08,020
We've set up this demonstration to show you

388
00:25:08,021 --> 00:25:10,840
the effects of friction and how the antitraction material

389
00:25:10,841 --> 00:25:12,080
negates that.

390
00:25:12,081 --> 00:25:14,680
This steel block weighs about 20 pounds.

391
00:25:14,681 --> 00:25:17,920
Up here on the dry part of the wood, it doesn't move.

392
00:25:17,921 --> 00:25:20,360
From here down, we've coated it with anti-attraction material.

393
00:25:20,361 --> 00:25:22,960
So as you can see, as I push it onto that,

394
00:25:22,961 --> 00:25:24,320
it will slide all the way down.

395
00:25:26,460 --> 00:25:29,360
To assess the effectiveness of this slippery goo,

396
00:25:29,361 --> 00:25:32,100
technicians have sprayed it inside this tented area

397
00:25:32,101 --> 00:25:36,900
that contains asphalt, concrete, and tile surfaces.

398
00:25:36,901 --> 00:25:38,800
I'm a field testing technician.

399
00:25:38,801 --> 00:25:40,580
I've been doing this for a number of years.

400
00:25:40,581 --> 00:25:46,260
And I've got a safety harness that's supposed to keep me from hitting the concrete.

401
00:25:46,800 --> 00:25:50,860
But as you can see, it's even hard for me to walk on this.

402
00:25:54,560 --> 00:25:57,780
This is the man portable system for the mobility denial system.

403
00:25:58,360 --> 00:26:00,140
It's a backpack unit, as you can see.

404
00:26:00,220 --> 00:26:02,160
It carries five gallons of water in this tank.

405
00:26:02,640 --> 00:26:06,220
On the back here is a compressed air cylinder, which operates an air pump,

406
00:26:06,221 --> 00:26:11,220
pumping the water through these hoses over to the nozzle.

407
00:26:11,320 --> 00:26:13,260
Anti-traction material is housed here.

408
00:26:13,360 --> 00:26:14,660
It's kept dry.

409
00:26:14,760 --> 00:26:16,960
Water and powder come out of this nozzle

410
00:26:17,060 --> 00:26:20,000
and mix in the air as it's reaching its objective.

411
00:26:20,100 --> 00:26:23,240
The strange goo can also turn any dirt or grass surface

412
00:26:23,340 --> 00:26:26,800
into a slippery nightmare.

413
00:26:26,900 --> 00:26:28,980
This intrepid volunteer treading on the stuff

414
00:26:29,080 --> 00:26:31,840
for the first time is learning that the hard way.

415
00:26:36,220 --> 00:26:46,340
To coat large surfaces, engineers designed a Humvee-mounted dispersal system under military

416
00:26:46,341 --> 00:26:47,340
guidelines.

417
00:26:47,341 --> 00:26:54,840
It contains a 300-gallon tank of water and approximately 250 pounds of the anti-traction

418
00:26:54,841 --> 00:26:58,780
material which is located in the hopper unit.

419
00:26:58,781 --> 00:27:02,140
The unit comprises of a water pump and an air compressor.

420
00:27:02,141 --> 00:27:07,540
The air compressor delivers the powder to the nozzle, and the water pump obviously pushes

421
00:27:07,541 --> 00:27:09,140
the water to the nozzle.

422
00:27:09,141 --> 00:27:14,760
The amount of material on this vehicle is capable of covering approximately a football

423
00:27:14,761 --> 00:27:18,940
field with the anti-traction material.

424
00:27:18,941 --> 00:27:23,460
The moment this van tries to traverse the sprayed area, the driver immediately has trouble

425
00:27:23,461 --> 00:27:26,400
continuing forward.

426
00:27:26,401 --> 00:27:31,460
As the tires spin, the material adheres to them, assuring no friction between the tires

427
00:27:31,461 --> 00:27:32,900
in the concrete road surface.

428
00:27:35,020 --> 00:27:38,300
It makes no difference if it's a rear-wheel drive,

429
00:27:38,440 --> 00:27:40,900
front-wheel drive, four-wheel drive vehicle.

430
00:27:41,120 --> 00:27:44,920
It's equally effective on all type of rubber-tired vehicles

431
00:27:44,921 --> 00:27:47,700
on a concrete or asphalt surface.

432
00:27:49,060 --> 00:27:51,260
This gooey slime proves that a weapon

433
00:27:51,261 --> 00:27:53,220
doesn't have to be deadly to be effective.

434
00:27:54,200 --> 00:27:56,120
Sometimes, weird suffices,

435
00:27:56,460 --> 00:27:59,080
which is why we slid it into the number five spot

436
00:27:59,081 --> 00:27:59,781
in our countdown.

437
00:28:01,460 --> 00:28:04,600
Our next strange entry is both weird and deadly.

438
00:28:05,460 --> 00:28:11,040
Dropping in at number four, one of the strangest bombs ever created, the Dam Buster.

439
00:28:14,540 --> 00:28:20,080
This bizarre weapon of World War II evolved as British war planners tried to solve a vexing problem.

440
00:28:21,420 --> 00:28:25,220
How to destroy key dams, supplying power to the German war machine.

441
00:28:26,440 --> 00:28:30,360
Dropping a bomb on a very narrow dam is nearly impossible to do.

442
00:28:30,361 --> 00:28:34,660
The bomb has to come right down and hit right on the edge of the dam, or it will do no good.

443
00:28:35,360 --> 00:28:40,160
The other way of destroying a dam is to fire a torpedo through the water into the side of the dam,

444
00:28:40,320 --> 00:28:43,320
but Germany had erected torpedo nets, making that impossible.

445
00:28:44,800 --> 00:28:49,340
British aircraft designer Barnes-Wallace came up with the unconventional solution.

446
00:28:50,260 --> 00:28:55,880
Wallace thought up this great idea where if we package the bomb again in a unique delivery system,

447
00:28:55,881 --> 00:29:00,280
we could drop it out of a plane and have it skip across the water.

448
00:29:00,360 --> 00:29:03,020
not sink into the water, but skip across the water

449
00:29:03,021 --> 00:29:06,700
until it hit the dam structure itself, and then detonate.

450
00:29:09,100 --> 00:29:12,060
Wallace's final design was a cylindrical bomb

451
00:29:12,061 --> 00:29:15,380
50 inches in diameter, 60 inches long,

452
00:29:15,680 --> 00:29:19,440
and filled with 6,600 pounds of powerful explosives.

453
00:29:21,340 --> 00:29:24,500
For the mission, it was determined that each Lancaster bomber

454
00:29:24,501 --> 00:29:27,500
needed to be flying at 220 miles an hour,

455
00:29:27,501 --> 00:29:32,920
just 60 feet above the water and 425 yards from the dam

456
00:29:32,921 --> 00:29:34,840
at the instant the bomb was dropped.

457
00:29:35,920 --> 00:29:38,860
Prior to its release, the bomb mounted on pivots

458
00:29:38,861 --> 00:29:43,960
was spun at over 500 RPM by a small motor built into the bomb bay.

459
00:29:45,240 --> 00:29:50,760
It was incredibly important that the dam buster bomb rotate backwards.

460
00:29:50,980 --> 00:29:52,960
It had to be designed to do that.

461
00:29:53,420 --> 00:29:57,040
If it were to rotate forward, then as it struck the dam,

462
00:29:57,041 --> 00:29:59,100
it would simply go up and over the dam,

463
00:29:59,200 --> 00:30:01,380
over on the other side and blow up harmlessly.

464
00:30:02,220 --> 00:30:05,840
But by rotating backward, when it struck the dam

465
00:30:05,841 --> 00:30:07,880
after it was bouncing across the water,

466
00:30:08,060 --> 00:30:11,780
it would actually go down into the water and then blow up.

467
00:30:13,080 --> 00:30:16,200
During the night raid on March 16, 1943,

468
00:30:16,620 --> 00:30:20,600
the bizarre bomb breached two dams and damaged a third.

469
00:30:22,100 --> 00:30:25,740
An unqualified historical success that earns the dam buster

470
00:30:25,741 --> 00:30:27,640
the number four spot on our countdown.

471
00:30:29,840 --> 00:30:32,020
A weird weapon that didn't make our countdown

472
