483
00:31:14,921 --> 00:31:22,640
Now let's turn some heads on the city streets with our number three oddity, the snail car.

484
00:31:22,641 --> 00:31:32,740
This automotive gastropod is the masterwork of artist and engineer John Seragardi.

485
00:31:32,741 --> 00:31:38,760
His Oakland, California company, Form and Reform, specializes in cars expressing an odd stylistic

486
00:31:38,761 --> 00:31:42,640
genre called steampunk.

487
00:31:42,641 --> 00:31:47,460
Steampunk applies an antiquated Victorian aesthetic to modern technology.

488
00:31:47,461 --> 00:31:49,460
These are weird machines.

489
00:31:49,461 --> 00:31:51,420
are not things you would see in the shopping mall

490
00:31:51,421 --> 00:31:54,240
or driving down the street on your way to work.

491
00:31:54,800 --> 00:31:57,200
The actual name of our number three oddity

492
00:31:57,201 --> 00:31:58,860
is the Golden Mean Art Car.

493
00:31:59,600 --> 00:32:01,180
But to the casual onlooker,

494
00:32:01,520 --> 00:32:03,040
the snail car seems more fitting.

495
00:32:03,520 --> 00:32:04,740
This is the Golden Mean.

496
00:32:04,741 --> 00:32:06,960
It's a giant iron snail car

497
00:32:06,961 --> 00:32:11,200
made on a 1966-67 VW Bug.

498
00:32:11,500 --> 00:32:14,060
This was a honeydew project from my wife

499
00:32:14,061 --> 00:32:16,060
who wanted a giant snail.

500
00:32:17,200 --> 00:32:19,440
Built to California Department of Motor Vehicles,

501
00:32:19,460 --> 00:32:24,460
The snail car is street legal with a top speed of 55 miles an hour.

502
00:32:27,460 --> 00:32:29,460
And did we mention that it breathes fire?

503
00:32:42,460 --> 00:32:45,460
Starting with just the chassis and engine of the VW Bug,

504
00:32:45,461 --> 00:32:50,394
Buck, Sara Gardie built the snail's frame and custom designs.

505
00:32:50,395 --> 00:32:52,820
To gain the look and feel of a

506
00:32:52,821 --> 00:32:57,902
true steampunk aesthetic, he went back to a traditional form of metalworking.

507
00:32:57,903 --> 00:32:58,760
I incorporate

508
00:32:58,761 --> 00:33:01,027
a lot of blacksmithing into the work that I do.

509
00:33:01,028 --> 00:33:02,860
I like the organic feel that it gives,

510
00:33:03,020 --> 00:33:06,940
a hand-touched, you can tell that it's not just come out of the processing machine.

511
00:33:08,160 --> 00:33:11,588
It gives my work an edge. It's not just fabricated.

512
00:33:11,589 --> 00:33:14,680
There's also some really great handwork in it.

513
00:33:15,460 --> 00:33:21,020
Saragardi added more than 2,000 pounds of new sheet metal and steel to the existing

514
00:33:21,021 --> 00:33:23,180
chassis.

515
00:33:23,181 --> 00:33:26,520
He also outfitted the car with an air ride system.

516
00:33:26,521 --> 00:33:30,060
A flip of a switch raises or lowers it to adjust to the number of passengers.

517
00:33:30,061 --> 00:33:33,860
Depending on how many people I have in here, I've had up to 19 people.

518
00:33:33,861 --> 00:33:38,700
I can turn up to 120 PSI and still maintain suspension.

519
00:33:38,701 --> 00:33:40,460
And how about those flame throwing eyes?

520
00:33:40,461 --> 00:33:41,460
Fire.

521
00:33:41,461 --> 00:33:45,800
One of the big features of the Snail ARCAR is fire coming out of its eye stalks.

522
00:33:45,801 --> 00:33:48,640
We have a liquid fuel propane source.

523
00:33:48,641 --> 00:33:52,740
This fuel is boiled off at room temperature and converted to gas, which we're storing

524
00:33:52,741 --> 00:33:54,280
inside of here.

525
00:33:54,281 --> 00:33:58,060
I have a valve that I can control that gas when it comes out.

526
00:33:58,061 --> 00:34:00,460
By pulling on that, it releases gas out the top.

527
00:34:00,461 --> 00:34:05,520
I have a separate system that's feeding the pilot light that's up here a needle valve

528
00:34:05,521 --> 00:34:08,460
to control how much gas I want out of that.

529
00:34:08,461 --> 00:34:10,940
The tank is housed in the neck of the Snail.

530
00:34:10,941 --> 00:34:13,200
